1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,432
Think three months of expenses is enough?

2
00:00:06,432 --> 00:00:12,864
For most families that number is dangerously low.

3
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:19,296
The standard advice says save three months.

4
00:00:19,296 --> 00:00:25,728
But the average job search now takes five months,

5
00:00:25,728 --> 00:00:32,160
and rent alone can wipe out a month of savings in a week.

6
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:38,592
When you add healthcare, car repairs, and a single emergency room visit,

7
00:00:38,592 --> 00:00:45,024
that three month cushion disappears before you even find a new job.

8
00:00:45,024 --> 00:00:51,456
Financial planners now recommend six to nine months of bare-bones expenses,

9
00:00:51,456 --> 00:00:57,888
Start with one extra month this year. That single month is the difference between panic and stability.

